id: pm-memory-child-checkpoint-rollback
title: Support guarded recovery from a standalone native memory checkpoint
description: A real tracker confirmed that direct update-many rollback of a child checkpoint exits 5 because the memory verification guard refuses the inverse. Rolling back the combined checkpoint restores the same row because that path scopes the SDK-proven inverse. A failed combined publication can leave only child checkpoint IDs in the receipt.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-20T15:44:34.519Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T15:44:34.519Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Provide a recovery path from the reported child checkpoint IDs that verifies native history and current postimages and retains other mutation guards.
parent: pm-memory-recall-freshness
